      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Odeh La-Él” sings to the waking soul, calling on it to return to the service of the Divine. Not much is known about the author, שמעיה קוסון (R’ Shamayah Ḳosson). He lived in the 16th century in Morocco. The poem gained widespread acceptance and has been popular among Israeli singers. It is unique since it is addressed to the soul rather than to the Divine.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
